          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "DeepSeek V4 API priced 97% below OpenAI's GPT-5.5, threatening global AI pricing norms",
            "articleSection": "Daily Utility",
            "abstract": "Chinese AI firm DeepSeek has slashed API pricing for its new V4 model to as low as $0.14 per million input tokens for cached requests, a level the company says is 97% cheaper than OpenAI's GPT-5.5. DeepSeek also reduced prices for cache-hit inputs to one-tenth of previous levels, a move that could force rival AI providers to respond with their own cuts. The pricing announcement follows the release of DeepSeek V4's preview, which features longer context windows and open-source weights.",
            "url": "https://www.scmp.com/tech/tech-trends/article/3351595/chinas-deepseek-prices-new-v4-ai-model-97-below-openais-gpt-55?utm_source=rss_feed",
            "publisher": {
